# WiFi Authentication Loop and MCU Timeout Investigation
# Date: 2026-01-12 22:10
# Kernel: 6.18.4-3-cachyos-wifi-fix (with 17 MT7925 patches)
# Status: SUSPICIOUS - No crash but unusual behavior

## Summary
After booting into patched kernel 6.18.4-3-cachyos-wifi-fix, WiFi entered an
authentication failure loop. MCU timeout occurred but recovered gracefully.
No kernel panic or NULL pointer crash (patches appear to be working).

## Key Observations
1. MCU command timeout occurred at ~1447s after boot
2. Driver recovered by reloading firmware automatically
3. Authentication failures with status 37 (SAE/WPA3 rejection)
4. Association denied (code=1) on some APs
5. Connection profile had pinned BSSID to weaker AP

## What Fixed It
- Cleared pinned BSSID from connection profile:
  nmcli connection modify "Bowling IoT Devices" 802-11-wireless.bssid ""
- Connected to stronger AP (DE:B3:70:F8:9E:7C on channel 6)
- WiFi working with excellent signal (-26 dBm)

## Suspicious Aspects
- Why did MCU timeout occur?
- Why were multiple APs rejecting authentication with status 37?
- Was there firmware/driver state corruption?
- Should investigate if this is related to roaming logic

