## Connection Profile Issue
The connection had a pinned BSSID:
802-11-wireless.bssid: DE:B3:70:F8:89:50

This AP (channel 1, 90% signal) was having issues while a stronger AP
(DE:B3:70:F8:9E:7C, channel 6, 100% signal) was available.

## Resolution
Cleared BSSID and reconnected:
$ nmcli connection modify "Bowling IoT Devices" 802-11-wireless.bssid ""
$ nmcli device wifi connect "Bowling IoT Devices" bssid DE:B3:70:F8:9E:7C

## Final State
Connected to de:b3:70:f8:9e:7c (on wlan0)
    SSID: Bowling IoT Devices
    freq: 2437.0
    signal: -26 dBm
    tx bitrate: 130.0 MBit/s MCS 15

Ping to 8.8.8.8: 2/2 packets received, ~100ms RTT

## Notes for Future Investigation
- Status 37 = SAE hash-to-element rejection (WPA3 issue?)
- MCU timeout Message 00020016 - what command is this?
- Consider if roaming between APs triggered the timeout
- Patches prevented crash but didn't prevent the timeout itself
